A||||4||ChopTop||Fuel filter leak or gas line leak???||||1||
Z||000000||ChopTop||11-20-2001||12:08 PM||||Hi folks, well we had to have our 88 coupe 4cylinder towed to our mechanic last night.  He replace the fuel filter couple weeks ago when it was stalling out, turned out the engine control module was our stalling problem.  Now it's developed a gas leak, I crawled under the car and it definitely seems to be leaking from the new fuel filter.  Our mechanic said it could possible be the fuel lines, and he isn't sure they are still available.<BR>I'm hoping the fuel filter just needs to be tighten.  Does anyone know if fuel lines are still available for our cars?<BR>Thanks in advance.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||11-20-2001||12:34 PM||||The mechanic may have fatigued the filter around the the hex when putting it in.  I had one crack from vibration and noticed the replacements are cheap, the metal is stretched thin near the hex fitting.  Could very well be that the threads aren't sealing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||11-20-2001||02:38 PM||||My mechanic twisted my fuel intake line irreparably.  He tried to gfind a replacement to no avail (including the J/Y)so he made one from flexible stainless - looks and works great!<P>Wish all my lines had to be replaced with this stuff!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||12
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-20-2001||04:21 PM||||The fuel lines must still be available as I had a leaking one replaced only a couple of months ago.  As I remember, the part wasn't all that expensive, but the labor was.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||beer_stud_21||11-20-2001||05:35 PM||||Disconnect the fuel line from the frame and run your fingers over the length of it.  Especially where it comes in contact with the little clamps that hold it to the frame.  When I got my car it had a few holes rubbed in the lines.  But since I'm a cheap bastard I fixed it with JB weld.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> worked good.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
